     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. 1600 mg four times daily (6,400 mg/day) is well above any recognized ibuprofen dosing. I don't know of a clinical setting where that dose has a favorable risk-benefit balance, and it carries a real risk of serious harm. The harms include GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. I'd rather not put it in the system, where it could be given before anyone catches it.\n\nI can enter any of these right now:\n- **Ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum labeled dose)\n- **Ibuprofen 600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **Ibuprofen 400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day)\n\nIf you need more analgesia or anti-inflammatory effect than these give, I can enter a multimodal regimen instead, such as scheduled acetaminophen with ibuprofen at the maximum dose.\n\nIf you think this dose is justified, for example under a protocol, please arrange it directly with pharmacy. That way it gets independent clinical review and proper monitoring, and doesn't come from me."
      }
